  "conclusion": "Pinned mainnet reads prove the deployed Avalanche OFT has the Ethereum adapter as its trusted peer, with the adapter reciprocally trusting that Avalanche OFT and wrapping issuer-authenticated Ethereum PEPE. Verified source shows the Ethereum adapter inherits LayerZero OFTAdapter (locking/unlocking underlying ERC-20) and the Avalanche token inherits LayerZero OFT. This is third-party bridge identity evidence, not issuer endorsement or a bridge security audit. Official operator attribution remains unresolved: actual adapter owner differs from the LayerZero-registered v1 and v2 PEPE adapters (see pepe-bridge-operator-readings.json); this proves origin only and is not sufficient to activate a trusted default deployment.",
